  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nAn upper ridge over the western states will build into Montana\nthis week with temperatures warming into Friday. Look for highs in\nthe 90s in most areas today. On Friday highs will be in the 90s\nnorth and near 100 south. \n\nA weak frontal system this evening will bring a slight chance for\nshowers and thunderstorms this evening. \n\nWest winds will increase on Friday behind this front as a surface\nlow passes east to the northeast of us. It looks like fuels will \nquickly dry and will be susceptible to burn, therefore a Fire \nWeather Watch remains in effect for Friday. West winds will \nlikely be strong enough to require a Lake Wind Advisory for Fort \nPeck Lake on Friday. \n\nA Extreme Heat Watch remains in effect for Friday through Sunday \nas nighttime lows will also not be cool enough for recovery for \nsensitive people. It looks like Saturday will be the hottest day \nwith most areas above 100 for highs. Winds will be lighter winds \non Saturday but slightly lower humidities will keep the Fire \nWeather concerns alive.\n\nFlow aloft turns SW on Saturday and a wave Saturday evening will\nbring chances for showers and thunderstorms mainly south of the\nMissouri River. \n\nSunday highs will be a few degrees lower that Saturday but still\nnear 100 in most areas to keep heat and fire weather concerns\ngoing. \nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nAdded thunderstorm chances to the forecast this evening and\nincreased wind speeds a few mph on Friday. No other changes to\nNBM. \n\nModerate confidence that there will be a thunderstorm somewhere in\nnortheast Montana this evening but low confidence on timing any\nspecific storm. High confidence on breezy west winds on Friday and\non the heat this weekend.",
